### Page 1 of 2

```text
RESOLUTION NO. _______________

ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION TO NAME A TRIANGLE SHAPED PARCEL OF REAL
PROPERTY LOCATED AT THE INTERSECTION OF RANDALL AVENUE,
WEST 32ND STREET AND DEY AVENUE ‘BILL DUBOIS MEMORIAL
PARK.’”

WHEREAS, the late Bill Dubois was born in Cheyenne Wyoming and taught in the
Cheyenne Schools for thirty seven years; and

WHEREAS, Bill Dubois co-authored many papers and articles about the history of
Cheyenne; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body is aware that Bill Dubois was the descendant of Esther
Hobart Morris, the first woman judge in the modern world, E.A. Slack, considered to be the main
father of Cheyenne Frontier Days, and William R. Dubois, an architect of many structures in
Cheyenne including seven homes in the Historic Dubois Block located near the triangle park;
and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body is aware that the late Bill Dubois served the Cheyenne
community in many ways, for many years, and was the recipient of many honors for his
contributions; and

WHEREAS, the City owns real property located at the intersection of Randall Avenue,
West 32nd Street and Dey Avenue, where a triangle park exists; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body wishes to acknowledge Bill Dubois’ many
contributions to Cheyenne and have been presented with a petition of 300 signatures of
community support of naming the aforesaid triangle park after him; and

WHEREAS, it is appropriate for governmental entities to name public facilities after
civic contributors in recognition of their efforts; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body believes it most fitting to name the above mentioned
existing triangle park the “Bill Dubois Memorial Park,” in recognition of Mr. Dubois’s
contribution to the enrichment of the City of Cheyenne, and its residents.

NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, that the property owned by the City of Cheyenne located at the
intersection of Randall Avenue, West 32nd Street and Dey Avenue, is hereby named the “Bill
Dubois Memorial Park.”

By Stefanie Boster at 8:57 pm, May 01, 2022
```

